def second_largest(nums):
    if len(nums) < 2:
        raise ValueError("need at least two elements")
    first = second = float('-inf')
    for n in nums:
        if n > first:
            second = first
            first = n
        elif n > second:
            second = n
    return second
```

One pass, tracking the largest and second largest seen so far. Since you said the values are distinct, the `elif` never hits an equal value, but if duplicates ever show up it still skips them correctly, so a repeated max won't be returned as the second largest.

Time O(n), space O(1).

